            </section>
            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear Colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital admission of your 84-year-old male patient from 6th to 7th December 2007. He was admitted due to an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD). On admission, clinical examination revealed decreased air entry bilaterally with expiratory wheeze. Oxygen saturation was reduced at rest. Arterial blood gas analysis confirmed hypoxaemic respiratory failure. Chest X-ray showed hyperinflation consistent with known COPD without consolidation. Blood tests revealed mild inflammatory markers. The patient was treated with supplemental oxygen therapy, nebulised bronchodilators (salbutamol and ipratropium), and a course of systemic corticosteroids. He responded well to treatment with improvement in symptoms and oxygen saturation. He is discharged home in a stable condition. Please ensure continued follow-up and review of his inhaler technique and maintenance therapy. Yours sincerely.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
